<section id="S1a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">A </span>Proofs of Results</h2>

<div id="S1a.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We restate and prove Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 2.1. ‣ 2.2 Tractability through 𝑘-ary dependencies ‣ 2 Janossy Pooling ‣ Janossy Pooling: Learning Deep Permutation-invariant Functions for Variable-size Inputs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1a.p2.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S2.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 2.1. ‣ 2.2 Tractability through 𝑘-ary dependencies ‣ 2 Janossy Pooling ‣ Janossy Pooling: Learning Deep Permutation-invariant Functions for Variable-size Inputs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S1a.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define two permutations <math id="S1a.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi,\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi_{|{\bm{h}}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi,\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi_{|{\bm{h}}|}</annotation></semantics></math> that agree on the
first <math id="S1a.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> elements as <math id="S1a.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="S1a.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-equivalent</span><span id="S1a.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text">. Such permutations satisfy
<math id="S1a.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k}\!\!({\bm{h}}_{\pi});\bm{\theta}^{(f)})=\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k}\!\!({\bm{h}}_{\pi^{\prime}});\bm{\theta}^{(f)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.418em">=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k}\!\!({\bm{h}}_{\pi});\bm{\theta}^{(f)})=\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k}\!\!({\bm{h}}_{\pi^{\prime}});\bm{\theta}^{(f)})</annotation></semantics></math>.
These two permutations belong to the same equivalence class, containing
a total of <math id="S1a.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(|{\bm{h}}|-k)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(|{\bm{h}}|-k)!</annotation></semantics></math> permutations (obtained by permuting the last <math id="S1a.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(|{\bm{h}}|-k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(|{\bm{h}}|-k)</annotation></semantics></math>
elements). Overall, we then have a total of <math id="S1a.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\bm{h}}|!/(|{\bm{h}}|-k)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\bm{h}}|!/(|{\bm{h}}|-k)!</annotation></semantics></math> equivalence
classes. Write the set of equivalence classes as <math id="S1a.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{|{\bm{h}}|}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{|{\bm{h}}|}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
represent each by one of its elements. Then,</span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}};\bm{\theta}^{(f)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}};\bm{\theta}^{(f)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{\pi\in\Pi_{|{\bm{h}}|}}\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k}\!\!({\bm{h}}_{\pi});\bm{\theta}^{(f)})=\frac{(|{\bm{h}}|-k)!}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{\pi\in\Pi_{|{\bm{h}}|}^{k}}\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}\big(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k}\!\!({\bm{h}}_{\pi});\bm{\theta}^{(f)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{\pi\in\Pi_{|{\bm{h}}|}}\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k}\!\!({\bm{h}}_{\pi});\bm{\theta}^{(f)})=\frac{(|{\bm{h}}|-k)!}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{\pi\in\Pi_{|{\bm{h}}|}^{k}}\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}\big(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k}\!\!({\bm{h}}_{\pi});\bm{\theta}^{(f)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1a.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">is now a summation over only <math id="S1a.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\bm{h}}|!/(|{\bm{h}}|-k)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\bm{h}}|!/(|{\bm{h}}|-k)!</annotation></semantics></math> terms. We can conclude that</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}};\bm{\theta}^{(f)})=\frac{(|{\bm{h}}|-k)!}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{(i_{1},i_{2},\ldots,i_{k})\in{\mathbb{I}}_{|{\bm{h}}|}}\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}\big(|{\bm{h}}|,({h}_{i_{1}},{h}_{i_{2}},\ldots,{h}_{i_{k}});\bm{\theta}^{(f)}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded></mrow></mrow><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}};\bm{\theta}^{(f)})=\frac{(|{\bm{h}}|-k)!}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{(i_{1},i_{2},\ldots,i_{k})\in{\mathbb{I}}_{|{\bm{h}}|}}\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}\big(|{\bm{h}}|,({h}_{i_{1}},{h}_{i_{2}},\ldots,{h}_{i_{k}});\bm{\theta}^{(f)}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1a.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1a.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we restate and prove the remaining portion of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.2 Tractability through 𝑘-ary dependencies ‣ 2 Janossy Pooling ‣ Janossy Pooling: Learning Deep Permutation-invariant Functions for Variable-size Inputs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.
See <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.2 Tractability through 𝑘-ary dependencies ‣ 2 Janossy Pooling ‣ Janossy Pooling: Learning Deep Permutation-invariant Functions for Variable-size Inputs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S1a.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">(<math id="S1a.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{k-1}\subset\mathcal{F}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{k-1}\subset\mathcal{F}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>): Consider any element
<math id="S1a.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}\in\mathcal{F}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}\in\mathcal{F}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and write <math id="S1a.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}(|{\bm{h}}|,~\cdot~;\bm{\theta}^{(f)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.330em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}(|{\bm{h}}|,~\cdot~;\bm{\theta}^{(f)})</annotation></semantics></math> for its
associated Janossy function.
For any sequence <math id="S1a.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1a.p5.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k-1}\!\!({\bm{h}});\bm{\theta}^{(f)})=\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k-1}\!\!(\downarrow_{k}\!\!({\bm{h}}));\bm{\theta}^{(f)}):=\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{+}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k}\!\!({\bm{h}});\bm{\theta}^{(f)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.418em">=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.418em">:=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><msub><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><mo>+</mo></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k-1}\!\!({\bm{h}});\bm{\theta}^{(f)})=\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k-1}\!\!(\downarrow_{k}\!\!({\bm{h}}));\bm{\theta}^{(f)}):=\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{+}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k}\!\!({\bm{h}});\bm{\theta}^{(f)})</annotation></semantics></math>, where the function
<math id="S1a.p5.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>
looks at its first <math id="S1a.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> elements.
Thus,</span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}};\bm{\theta}^{(f)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}};\bm{\theta}^{(f)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{\pi\in\Pi_{|{\bm{h}}|}}\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\downarrow_{k-1\&gt;}\!\!}({\bm{h}}_{\pi});\bm{\theta}^{(f)})=\frac{1}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{\pi\in\Pi_{|{\bm{h}}|}}\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{+}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k}\!\!({\bm{h}}_{\pi});\bm{\theta}^{(f)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><msub><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><mo>+</mo></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{\pi\in\Pi_{|{\bm{h}}|}}\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\downarrow_{k-1\&gt;}\!\!}({\bm{h}}_{\pi});\bm{\theta}^{(f)})=\frac{1}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{\pi\in\Pi_{|{\bm{h}}|}}\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{+}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k}\!\!({\bm{h}}_{\pi});\bm{\theta}^{(f)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}};\bm{\theta}^{(f)}),\vskip-10.0pt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}};\bm{\theta}^{(f)}),\vskip-10.0pt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1a.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S1a.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Janossy function associated with <math id="S1a.p5.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and thus belongs to
<math id="S1a.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">(<math id="S1a.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{k}\not\subset\mathcal{F}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⊄</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{k}\not\subset\mathcal{F}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>): the case where <math id="S1a.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> is trivial, so assume <math id="S1a.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. We will demonstrate the existence of <math id="S1a.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}\in\mathcal{F}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}\in\mathcal{F}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>
such that <math id="S1a.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}\neq\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}\neq\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for all
<math id="S1a.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}\in\mathcal{F}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}\in\mathcal{F}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S1a.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1a.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> be associated with <math id="S1a.p6.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1a.p6.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">It suffices to consider
<math id="S1a.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\bm{h}}|=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\bm{h}}|=k</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S1a.p7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{k}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}}_{\pi};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k})=\prod_{l=1}^{|{\bm{h}}|}{h}_{\pi(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><msub><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{k}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}}_{\pi};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k})=\prod_{l=1}^{|{\bm{h}}|}{h}_{\pi(l)}</annotation></semantics></math>
whence <math id="S1a.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k})=\prod_{l=1}^{|{\bm{h}}|}{h}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k})=\prod_{l=1}^{|{\bm{h}}|}{h}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, for any <math id="S1a.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="S1a.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k-1})}{\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k-1})}{\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{\pi\in\Pi_{|{\bm{h}}|}}\dfrac{\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{k-1}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k-1}\!\!({\bm{h}}_{\pi});{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k-1})}{\prod_{l=1}^{|{\bm{h}}|}{h}_{l}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">↓</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{\pi\in\Pi_{|{\bm{h}}|}}\dfrac{\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{k-1}(|{\bm{h}}|,\downarrow_{k-1}\!\!({\bm{h}}_{\pi});{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k-1})}{\prod_{l=1}^{|{\bm{h}}|}{h}_{l}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{j=1}^{|{\bm{h}}|}\sum_{\tilde{\pi}\in\Pi_{\{1,\ldots,|{\bm{h}}|\}\setminus{j}}}\dfrac{\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{k-1}\big(|{\bm{h}}|,({\bm{h}}_{-j})_{\tilde{\pi}};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k-1}\big)}{\prod_{l=1}^{|{\bm{h}}|}{h}_{l}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{j=1}^{|{\bm{h}}|}\sum_{\tilde{\pi}\in\Pi_{\{1,\ldots,|{\bm{h}}|\}\setminus{j}}}\dfrac{\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{k-1}\big(|{\bm{h}}|,({\bm{h}}_{-j})_{\tilde{\pi}};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k-1}\big)}{\prod_{l=1}^{|{\bm{h}}|}{h}_{l}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1a.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S1a.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\{1,\ldots,|{\bm{h}}|\}\setminus{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\{1,\ldots,|{\bm{h}}|\}\setminus{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of permutation functions defined on <math id="S1a.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,2,\ldots,j-1,j+1,\ldots,|{\bm{h}}|\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,2,\ldots,j-1,j+1,\ldots,|{\bm{h}}|\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1a.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{h}}_{-j})_{\tilde{\pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{h}}_{-j})_{\tilde{\pi}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a permutation of the sequence <math id="S1a.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big({h}_{1},\ldots,{h}_{j-1},{h}_{j+1},\ldots,{h}_{|{\bm{h}}|}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big({h}_{1},\ldots,{h}_{j-1},{h}_{j+1},\ldots,{h}_{|{\bm{h}}|}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>. This can be written as</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{j=1}^{|{\bm{h}}|}\frac{1}{{h}_{j}}\underbrace{\Big(\sum_{\tilde{\pi}\in\Pi_{\{1,\ldots,|{\bm{h}}|\}\setminus{j}}}\dfrac{\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{k-1}\big(|{\bm{h}}|,({\bm{h}}_{-j})_{\tilde{\pi}};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k-1}\big)}{\prod_{l\neq j}{h}_{l}}\Big)}_{\text{denote by }a_{j,|{\bm{h}}|}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.265em;" width="0.265em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mpadded voffset="6.9pt"><mo mathsize="0.500em" stretchy="false">⇀</mo></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>denote by </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{j=1}^{|{\bm{h}}|}\frac{1}{{h}_{j}}\underbrace{\Big(\sum_{\tilde{\pi}\in\Pi_{\{1,\ldots,|{\bm{h}}|\}\setminus{j}}}\dfrac{\mathstrut\mkern 2.5muf\mkern-11.0mu\raise 6.88889pt\hbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\rightharpoonup$}_{k-1}\big(|{\bm{h}}|,({\bm{h}}_{-j})_{\tilde{\pi}};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k-1}\big)}{\prod_{l\neq j}{h}_{l}}\Big)}_{\text{denote by }a_{j,|{\bm{h}}|}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1a.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">therefore</span></p>
<table id="S1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dfrac{\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}}_{\pi};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k-1})}{\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}}_{\pi};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k})}=\frac{1}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{j=1}^{|{\bm{h}}|}\frac{1}{{h}_{j}}a_{j,|{\bm{h}}|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dfrac{\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}}_{\pi};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k-1})}{\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}(|{\bm{h}}|,{\bm{h}}_{\pi};{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{k})}=\frac{1}{|{\bm{h}}|!}\sum_{j=1}^{|{\bm{h}}|}\frac{1}{{h}_{j}}a_{j,|{\bm{h}}|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1a.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Now, <math id="S1a.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}=\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k-1}=\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$f$}}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only
if their quotient in equation <a href="#S1.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Proof. ‣ A Proofs of Results ‣ Janossy Pooling: Learning Deep Permutation-invariant Functions for Variable-size Inputs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> is unity for all <math id="S1a.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
But this is clearly not possible in general unless <math id="S1a.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>
is a singleton, which we have precluded in our assumptions.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2.2. ‣ 2.3 Tractability through Permutation Sampling ‣ 2 Janossy Pooling ‣ Janossy Pooling: Learning Deep Permutation-invariant Functions for Variable-size Inputs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> is repeated below and is followed by a more rigorous restatement.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p9.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S2.Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2.2. ‣ 2.3 Tractability through Permutation Sampling ‣ 2 Janossy Pooling ‣ Janossy Pooling: Learning Deep Permutation-invariant Functions for Variable-size Inputs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The following statement is similar to that in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yuille (2004)</a></cite>, which also provides intuition behind the theoretical assumptions, which are indeed quite general. See also <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Younes, 1999</a>)</cite>. This is a familiar application of stochastic approximation algorithms already used in training neural networks.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.1</span></span><span id="S1.Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="S1.Thmproposition1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>-SGD Convergence)<span id="S1.Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the <math id="S1.Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>-SGD algorithm in Definition <a href="#S2.Thmdefinition3" title="Definition 2.3 (𝜋-SGD). ‣ 2.3 Tractability through Permutation Sampling ‣ 2 Janossy Pooling ‣ Janossy Pooling: Learning Deep Permutation-invariant Functions for Variable-size Inputs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>.
If</span></p>
<ol id="S1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:.25in;">
<li id="S1.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">there exists a constant </span><math id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that for all </span><math id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-{\bm{G}}_{t}^{T}{\bm{\theta}}\leq M\|{\bm{\theta}}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-{\bm{G}}_{t}^{T}{\bm{\theta}}\leq M\|{\bm{\theta}}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,
where </span><math id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{G}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{G}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the true gradient for the full batch over all permutations,
</span><math id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{G}}_{t}=\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$J$}}}(\mathcal{D};{\bm{\theta}}^{(\rho)}_{t},{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{t},{\bm{\theta}}^{(h)}_{t})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mpadded voffset="-0.9pt"><mi>J</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{G}}_{t}=\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\overline{\overline{\lower 0.86108pt\hbox{$J$}}}(\mathcal{D};{\bm{\theta}}^{(\rho)}_{t},{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)}_{t},{\bm{\theta}}^{(h)}_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
where </span><math id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}\equiv({\bm{\theta}}^{(\rho)},{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)},{\bm{\theta}}^{(h)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}\equiv({\bm{\theta}}^{(\rho)},{\bm{\theta}}^{(f)},{\bm{\theta}}^{(h)})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and </span><math id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the optimum.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">there exists a constant </span><math id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that for all </span><math id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{t}[\|{\mathbf{Z}}_{t}\|_{2}^{2}]\leq\delta^{2}(1+\|{\bm{\theta}}_{t}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}_{t}\|_{2}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{t}[\|{\mathbf{Z}}_{t}\|_{2}^{2}]\leq\delta^{2}(1+\|{\bm{\theta}}_{t}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}_{t}\|_{2}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, where the expectation is taken with respect to all the data prior to step </span><math id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S1.Thmproposition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmproposition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the algorithm in equation <a href="#S2.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Definition 2.3 (𝜋-SGD). ‣ 2.3 Tractability through Permutation Sampling ‣ 2 Janossy Pooling ‣ Janossy Pooling: Learning Deep Permutation-invariant Functions for Variable-size Inputs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> converges to <math id="S1.Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝛉</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability one.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1a.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S1a.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1a.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we can show that <math id="S1a.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{t}[{\mathbf{Z}}_{t}]={\bm{G}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{t}[{\mathbf{Z}}_{t}]={\bm{G}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by equation <a href="#S2.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ 2.3 Tractability through Permutation Sampling ‣ 2 Janossy Pooling ‣ Janossy Pooling: Learning Deep Permutation-invariant Functions for Variable-size Inputs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, the linearity of the derivative operator, and the fact that the permutations are independently sampled for each training example in the mini-batch and are assumed independent of <math id="S1a.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
That equation <a href="#S2.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Definition 2.3 (𝜋-SGD). ‣ 2.3 Tractability through Permutation Sampling ‣ 2 Janossy Pooling ‣ Janossy Pooling: Learning Deep Permutation-invariant Functions for Variable-size Inputs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> converges to <math id="S1a.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is a consequence of our conditions and the supermartingale convergence theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grimmett &amp; Stirzaker, 2001</a>, pp. 481)</cite>.
The following argument follows <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yuille (2004)</a></cite>.
Let <math id="S1a.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}=\|{\bm{\theta}}_{t}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}=\|{\bm{\theta}}_{t}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1a.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{t}=\delta^{2}\eta_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{t}=\delta^{2}\eta_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S1a.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}=-\|{\bm{\theta}}_{t}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}(\delta^{2}\eta_{t}^{2}-2M\eta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}=-\|{\bm{\theta}}_{t}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}(\delta^{2}\eta_{t}^{2}-2M\eta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S1a.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive for a sufficiently large <math id="S1a.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S1a.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{\infty}B_{t}\leq\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{\infty}B_{t}\leq\infty</annotation></semantics></math> by our definition of <math id="S1a.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (Definition  <a href="#S2.Thmdefinition3" title="Definition 2.3 (𝜋-SGD). ‣ 2.3 Tractability through Permutation Sampling ‣ 2 Janossy Pooling ‣ Janossy Pooling: Learning Deep Permutation-invariant Functions for Variable-size Inputs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>).
We will demonstrate that <math id="S1a.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{t}[A_{t}]\leq A_{t-1}+B_{t-1}-C_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{t}[A_{t}]\leq A_{t-1}+B_{t-1}-C_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="S1a.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, in the Supplementary Material from which it follows that <math id="S1a.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to zero with probability one and <math id="S1a.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{\infty}C_{t}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{\infty}C_{t}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
We write</span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{t}\left[\|{\bm{\theta}}_{t}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{t}\left[\|{\bm{\theta}}_{t}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=E_{t}\left[\|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}-\eta_{t-1}{\mathbf{Z}}_{t-1}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=E_{t}\left[\|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}-\eta_{t-1}{\mathbf{Z}}_{t-1}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}-2\eta_{t-1}E_{t}[({\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star})^{T}{\mathbf{Z}}_{t-1}]+\eta_{t-1}^{2}E_{t}[\|{\mathbf{Z}}_{t-1}\|_{2}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}-2\eta_{t-1}E_{t}[({\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}-{\bm{\theta}}^{\star})^{T}{\mathbf{Z}}_{t-1}]+\eta_{t-1}^{2}E_{t}[\|{\mathbf{Z}}_{t-1}\|_{2}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
